# Purpose sentence

The homepage purpose sentence is the first thing under the site header, on phone, tablet, and desktop. It sits above the Daily News card and the rag-pic card so a visitor reads what the site is before those cards.

Keep that sentence in the `site-intro` section in `client/src/pages/Home.tsx`, and keep that section before the quick-access section. It stays full width of the page content (`max-w-7xl`). The cards may stack on a phone. They still come after the sentence.

Pass the sentence through `markTaxpayer()` so the word taxpayer keeps its standing treatment. In this sentence only, the opening word `Flush` and the word `flushable` are flush blue (`flush-accent-word`). Leave `bad flush` and every other flush word on the site alone.

```tsx
<section aria-label="About The Flush Report" className="site-intro">
  <p className="mx-auto max-w-7xl">
    The <span className="flush-accent-word">Flush</span>
    {markTaxpayer(" Report is a public news site about what happens after a bad flush. We cover the clogs, spills, and taxpayer bills that start when ")}
    <span className="flush-accent-word">flushable</span>
    {markTaxpayer(" wipes, rags, grease, and trash go down the toilet.")}
  </p>
</section>
```

Do not move the sentence beside the cards, inside a card, or down under Think Before You Flush.
